    },
    {
      "id": "execute-chapter", "label": "2. Claim and infer",
      "description": "A compatible runtime claims a leased, attempt-fenced job. GeneralAssistant calls the selected local engine or explicitly disclosed remote model. Provider choice does not transfer policy authority.",
      "entities": ["orchestrator", "runtime", "models"], "flows": ["assign", "inference"], "zones": ["authority-zone", "execution-zone"]
    },
    {
      "id": "tools-chapter", "label": "3. Gate every tool",
      "description": "BEFORE beacons obtain policy. The orchestrator reads bounded file previews on a private capability-protected endpoint. Bundled calls leave from the runtime; registered MCP/GitHub calls are mediated by the orchestrator. Only mcp-files consumes approvals over the return gRPC path.",
      "entities": ["runtime", "orchestrator", "bundled", "registered"], "flows": ["updates", "mcp-call", "consume", "proxy", "preview-cleanup"], "zones": ["authority-zone", "execution-zone"]
    },
    {
      "id": "team-chapter", "label": "4. Delegate without waiting in-run",
      "description": "Optional team.delegate creates a hidden child job, not another daemon. The parent yields the single default slot. Each child has its own tools, approvals and egress decision; all terminal child results join into one local continuation.",
      "entities": ["orchestrator", "durable", "runtime", "models"], "flows": ["persist", "assign", "updates", "inference"], "zones": ["authority-zone", "execution-zone"]
    },
    {
      "id": "reconcile-chapter", "label": "5. Reconcile and display",
      "description": "The orchestrator persists outcomes and streams them to Flutter. Reopen reads history and delegation records. Stop and deletion fence late work; mcp-files cleanup uses its separate private bearer. No committed external effect is undone.",
